<figure id="A5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span><span id="A5.T5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">“flash” register split (Gemma 2 9B).</span> Solo feature 3387
conflates the general sense of a sudden, brief occurrence with the proper-noun
sense of Adobe Flash software. The joint SAE separates them: feat. 63365
retains the sudden-event sense (<math id="A5.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varphi|\!=\!0.857" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.857</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varphi|\!=\!0.857</annotation></semantics></math>), while feat. 34102
isolates the Adobe Flash sense (<math id="A5.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varphi|\!=\!0.173" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.173</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varphi|\!=\!0.173</annotation></semantics></math>). Despite its low
<math id="A5.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varphi|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varphi|</annotation></semantics></math>—reflecting how rarely this sense fires—feat. 34102 achieves
the highest fuzzing score in the Gemma analysis (<math id="A5.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.725" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.725</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.725</annotation></semantics></math>), illustrating how
the decomposability penalty can liberate a rare but highly coherent sense
that the solo SAE submerges.</figcaption>
